# ===========================================================================
# The Reading Bridge — response headers
#
# Format rules enforced by Netlify (docs.netlify.com/manage/routing/headers and
# the "why are my _headers rules not working as expected" support guide):
#   * a path line starts at column 0, with NO leading spaces;
#   * every header line under it is indented by EXACTLY TWO SPACES;
#   * a path line and its header lines are consecutive — no blank line between.
# The public rules below previously had their header lines at column 0, which is
# not the documented syntax, so the indentation is corrected here alongside the
# new /admin/ rule.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Public site -----------------------------------------------------------
# Strict: self-hosted assets only, no inline script or style, no framing, no
# third-party connections at all.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-src 'none'; form-action 'self' mailto:

# --- The content editor at /admin/ ONLY ------------------------------------
# Decap CMS is a bundled single-page app. It is the one path that cannot live
# under the public policy above, so it gets its own PATH-SCOPED policy. The
# public rules are unchanged, and this rule never applies to a public page.
#
# Every relaxation below exists for a specific, named reason:
#   script-src 'self'                 admin/index.html has no inline script:
#                                     all four scripts are files under /admin/
#                                     (two vendored, two ours).
#   script-src 'unsafe-eval'          Decap's bundled AJV schema compiler builds
#                                     its validators with `new Function(...)`
#                                     (verified inside the vendored bundle).
#   script-src 'wasm-unsafe-eval'     Decap ships a WebAssembly WebP encoder
#                                     (vendor/*.wasm); compiling it needs this
#                                     token. It does NOT permit string eval.
#   style-src  'unsafe-inline'        Decap 2.0+ dropped static CSS for
#                                     CSS-in-JS (vendor/cms.css is an empty
#                                     placeholder that says so), so it injects
#                                     <style> elements at runtime.
#   img-src    data: blob:            inline data-URI art, and blob: previews
#                                     for locally chosen files.
#   font-src   data:                  fonts embedded in the injected CSS.
#   connect-src https://api.netlify.com
#                                     the Git Gateway / Netlify Identity API.
#                                     Authentication itself posts to
#                                     /.netlify/identity on THIS origin, which
#                                     'self' already covers; the vendored bundle
#                                     contains no identity.netlify.com reference,
#                                     so that host is deliberately NOT allowed.
#   frame-src  'self'                 Decap's editor-preview pane is a
#                                     same-origin iframe (window.open popups are
#                                     not governed by frame-src). The preview is
#                                     switched off in admin/config.yml, so this
#                                     is headroom rather than a requirement.
#
# Ordering: this block is deliberately placed AFTER the /* block, relying on
# Netlify applying the last matching rule for a given header name. If a deploy
# shows /admin/ still receiving the public CSP, move this block ABOVE the /*
# block and redeploy.
/admin/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.netlify.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-src 'self'; form-action 'self'
